--- a/docs/build.md
+++ b/docs/build.md
@@ -748,6 +748,68 @@ Follow the instructions [here](https://dawn.googlesource.com/dawn/+/refs/heads/m
 
 To read documentation for how to build on IBM Z & LinuxONE, [click here](./build-s390x.md)
 
+## RISC-V
+
+The riscv64 CPU backend selects its `-march` string from the following options. All
+of them are ignored unless the target is riscv64, and all are ignored when
+`GGML_CPU_ALL_VARIANTS` is enabled.
+
+| Option | Default | Notes |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `GGML_RVV` | `ON` | Vector extension (RVV 1.0). Turn `OFF` for cores without a vector unit. |
+| `GGML_RV_ZFH` | `ON` | Scalar half-precision floating point. |
+| `GGML_RV_ZVFH` | `ON` | Vector half-precision floating point. Requires `GGML_RVV`. |
+| `GGML_RV_ZVFBFWMA` | `OFF` | Vector BF16 widening multiply-add. Requires `GGML_RVV`. |
+| `GGML_RV_ZICBOP` | `ON` | Cache block prefetch. |
+| `GGML_RV_ZIHINTPAUSE` | `ON` | `pause` hint. |
+| `GGML_RV_ZBA` | `ON` | Address generation. Part of the RVA22/RVA23 baseline. |
+| `GGML_RV_ZBB` | `ON` | Basic bit manipulation. Part of the RVA22/RVA23 baseline. |
+| `GGML_XTHEADVECTOR` | `OFF` | T-Head vector extension, used instead of RVV 1.0. |
+
+The defaults target a current RVA23-class core. For older or narrower hardware,
+turn off whatever the core does not implement — executing an instruction from an
+unimplemented extension traps.
+
+### SpacemiT
+
+Cores implementing the SpacemiT IME matrix extension (e.g. the K1) can use
+hand-written matrix kernels via `-DGGML_CPU_RISCV64_SPACEMIT=ON`, together with
+`cmake/riscv64-spacemit-linux-gnu-gcc.cmake` and the vendor toolchain in
+`RISCV_ROOT_PATH`.
+
+### MIPS P8700
+
+The P8700 implements `RV64GC_Zba_Zbb`. It has no vector unit, no half-precision
+floating point, and provides `Xmipscbop` rather than `Zicbop`, so those options
+must be turned off:
+
+```sh
+cmake -B build \
+    -DGGML_RVV=OFF \
+    -DGGML_RV_ZFH=OFF \
+    -DGGML_RV_ZVFH=OFF \
+    -DGGML_RV_ZICBOP=OFF \
+    -DGGML_RV_ZBA=ON \
+    -DGGML_RV_ZBB=ON \
+    -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=$PWD/cmake/riscv64-mips-p8700-linux-gnu-gcc.cmake
+cmake --build build --config Release -j $(nproc)
+```
+
+The toolchain file uses the distribution cross compiler by default; set
+`RISCV_TOOLCHAIN_SUFFIX` to pick a specific version (e.g. `-14`), or set the
+`RISCV_ROOT_PATH` environment variable to use a standalone toolchain.
+
+The MIPS vendor extensions (`Xmipscmov`, `Xmipslsp`, `Xmipscbop`) are not part of
+the default `-march`, since not every toolchain accepts them. Add them with
+`-DMIPS_P8700_MARCH_EXTRA=_xmipscmov_xmipslsp_xmipscbop` on a toolchain that does.
+
+QEMU 10 and later model this core directly, which is enough to run the test
+suite without hardware:
+
+```sh
+qemu-riscv64 -L /usr/riscv64-linux-gnu -cpu mips-p8700 ./build/bin/test-backend-ops
+```
+
 ## OpenVINO
 
 [OpenVINO](https://docs.openvino.ai/) is an open-source toolkit for optimizing and deploying high-performance AI inference, specifically designed for Intel hardware (CPUs, GPUs, and NPUs).
